    Bug 2045220 - Add a contentLanguage property to NewMessageDetails. r=mkmelin

    messages.sendMessage() and messages.saveMessage() currently do not set the Content-Language
    header. Add an optional contentLanguage property (an array of free-form language
    tags) to NewMessageDetails, which is written verbatim to the header. When it is omitted,
    no Content-Language header is added.

    Callers can use the existing i18n.detectLanguage() to derive a tag from the message body,
    which should be converted to plain text first (via messengerUtilities.convertToPlainText)
    so markup does not influence the result.

    Adds test_content_language: an explicit contentLanguage is written verbatim, and no
    header is added when it is omitted.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D304959

